ook: aviation technical documents. Archivo + IBM Plex Mono, hairline grid, the tail-number lookup is the hero.\n\nB \u00b7 Atelier: bespoke upholstery. Bodoni Moda + Hanken Grotesk, full-bleed before/after hero, stitched seam line, dark portal band.\n\nC \u00b7 Altitude: evolve what we have. Fraunces + Manrope kept, bigger type, a pinned scroll story of the transformation, quieter lists instead of cards.\n\nAll three are interactive: try the tail lookup (A), drag the hero (B), click the stages (C)."},"t-lb":{"x":0,"y":30600,"text":"Logbook \u2014 chosen direction","kind":"title1","maxW":8000},"lb-note":{"x":8160,"y":33500,"w":460,"maxH":900,"fill":"orange","text":"Logbook is the chosen direction (Oct 20).\n\nThese boards replace Home, the Bonanza model page and the Start flow above. The drag-to-compare wiper moved out of the hero into its own full-width section on Home and the model page, and it is the reveal on Start step 5.\n\nThe remaining pages follow the same kit: plates, registers, mono data, ink rules, needle red only on the primary action."}},"designSystems":[{"title":"Air Sew","namespace":"air-sew","artifact":"https://claude.ai/artifact/GigKE6tXhV85PwfdoGf2PE","version":null,"copiedAt":"2026-10-20T02:10:00Z"}]}